:: Fishing Beach Catch
<<effects>>
<<if Weather.dayState is "day" and ($daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase is "finished" or $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase is undefined) and $rng gte 92 and $daily.fishing.seagullSteal is undefined>>
	<<fishingSeagullCaught $fishingHookedFish $bus>>
<<elseif $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase is "fishing" and $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.drunk gte 1 and $rng gte 80>>
	<<fishingBeachCaughtFisherDrunk>>
<<elseif beachCampfirePartyPresent() and $rng gte 75 and $daily.fishing.beach.partyFeed is undefined and canCookFish($fishingHookedFish.type)>>
	<<fishingBeachCaughtCampfireCook>>
<<else>>
	<<fishingBeachCaught>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Beach Reel
<<effects>>
<<set $fishingReelAttempts += 1>>

<<if $athleticsSuccess>>
	You brace against the rocks and heave, and you <<if $fishingReelAttempts gt 1>>finally<</if>> <span class="green">reel up the fish.</span><<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<include "Fishing Beach Catch">>
<<elseif $fishingReelAttempts gte 3 and random(1, 5) gte 4>>
	<<if $rng gte 80>>
		<<fishingBeachRodLost>>
	<<else>>
		<<fishingBeachLineSnapped>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $fishingReelAttempts is 1>>
		You haul back on your rod, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> strips your line right back off the reel. Your arms burn with the effort.<<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<<else>>
		You drag it closer, close enough to see its shape in the breakers, before it dives again, nearly pulling you off your feet.<<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _reelDifficultyMax to Math.clamp($fishingHookedFish.size * 10, 600, 1400)>>
	<<link [[Keep fighting it|Fishing Beach Reel]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty -250 _reelDifficultyMax>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Cut the line|Fishing Beach Cut Line]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Beach Cut Line
<<effects>>
You release the tension on your rod, letting your line go slack. The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, your line breaks free. Through the ripples, you catch a glimpse of it darting deeper, finally free.
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>


:: Widgets Fishing Beach Catch [widget]
<<widget "fishingBeachRodLost">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> gives one last violent pull and your rod is wrenched clean out of your hands, tumbling away into the waves.<<gstress>><<stress 4>><<handheldruined>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingBeachLineSnapped">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but your line goes taut, then <span class="red">snaps.</span> The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is gone, and your line goes slack.
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingBeachCaught">>
	<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, $bus)>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<<set _fishPropName to "caught-" + $fishingHookedFish.type>>
	<<wearProp _fishPropName>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<if _canEatFish>>
		It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Beach Keep]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Beach Throw Back]]>><</link>>
	<<if _canEatFish>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Beach Cat Eat]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>
